# Titan Orbit — Sphere-surface map

The playable map is the **outside of a sphere** at the world origin. Flying far enough around the shell brings you back to the same rocks. That is the wrap-around *feel*. There is **no** XZ torus, **no** `Wrap` of the ship, **no** display tiles, and **no** 9-tile collider copies.

Paired APIs: `SphericalMapEcs`, `SphericalMap`. Compatibility facades `ToroidalMapEcs` / `ToroidalMap` forward to geodesic math (display helpers are identity).

---

## One layer (do not invent a second)

| Layer | Behavior | API |
|-------|----------|-----|
| **Sim + presentation** | Every body has **one** world pose on the shell. Distances are **geodesics**. Local up is radial (away from center). | `SphericalMapEcs.GeodesicDistance`, `GeodesicDirection`, `GeodesicOffset`, `ProjectToSphere`, `LocalUp`, `FlattenToTangent` |

```csharp
// BAD — Euclidean chord through the globe
float d = math.distance(ship, planet);

// GOOD — great-circle on the shell
float d = SphericalMapEcs.GeodesicDistance(ship, planet, radius);

// BAD — extra tile copies or wrap of the local ship
transform.Position = ToroidalMapEcs.Wrap(transform.Position);
displayPos = ToroidalMapEcs.GetDisplayPosition(logical, ship, w, h);

// GOOD — one object, real pose; project movers back onto the shell
pos = SphericalMapEcs.ProjectToSphere(pos, radius);
```

`ProjectToSphere` keeps hulls / bullets / gems on the shell. It is **not** a teleport-to-other-edge wrap.

---

## Feature checklist (orbit, dock, transports, combat)

Any new range / target / spawn / magnet / orbit / unload logic must:

- [ ] Read `MapRadius` from `MapStateSingleton` / session meta (or `SphericalMapEcs` after bootstrap)
- [ ] Use **geodesic** distance / tangent direction — never raw `distance` for gameplay ranges
- [ ] Place moons / surface points with `OrbitOffsetWorld` / `SurfacePointToward` (planet local up, not world Y)
- [ ] Keep **one** GameObject / collider per body
- [ ] Constrain bullets and scripted movers onto the shell (`StepOnSphere` / re-project)
- [ ] Cursor aim: **near** sphere ray hit only (`SphericalMap.TryRaycastNear`) — never the far hemisphere

**Orbit ring:** membership = `PlanetOrbitMath.IsInOrbitRing(GeodesicDistance(...), inner, outer)`. Tangents use the planet's local up (`cross(LocalUp(planet), radial)`).

---

## Forbidden

- 9-tile collider copies, wrap-duplicate GameObjects, or display tiling
- Euclidean-only gameplay ranges (shots through the globe)
- Flattening aim / velocity onto world Y / XZ
- Inventing a silent map size or radius (never 1000×1000)
- Dual torus + sphere modes

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Gameplay math is geodesic / tangent
- [ ] All movers stay on the shell
- [ ] One object per body
- [ ] New systems document `MapRadius` source in comments
